{"step_index":1685,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T00:01:15Z","thinking":"**Investigating graph parameter relations**\n\nConsidering exploring the connection between the radius and the Roman domination number of a graph. A literature search, possibly via a script, could reveal existing results for $\\text{rad}(G)$ and $\\gamma_R(G)$. Recalling related graph parameters, and their relationship, it seems appropriate to query a resource for the standard relationships between diameter, radius, domination number, and Roman domination number. Standard inequality: $\\gamma(G) \\le ...$ is remembered.\n\n\n**Examining Path Graph Inequalities**\n\nFound the radius of a path graph $P_n$ is $\\lfloor n/2 \\rfloor$ and its domination number is $\\lceil n/3 \\rceil$. Calculated $\\gamma_R(P_6)$ to be 4 and observed that radius + 1 is less than or equal to $\\gamma_R$. Calculated a few values, radius+1 is usually greater than $\\gamma$.\n\nConfirmed the inequality $\\text{radius}(P_n) + 1 \\le \\gamma_R(P_n)$ through a series of example path graphs, with equality for $n = 2, 3, 4, 6$. The investigation now considers if this holds for other tree structures.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python3 -c \\\"\\nimport networkx as nx\\nfrom itertools import product\\n\\ndef roman_domination_number(G):\\n    n = G.number_of_nodes()\\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\\n    # find min weight of RDF\\n    min_w = 2 * n\\n    for assignment in product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\\n        w = sum(assignment)\\n        if w >= min_w:\\n            continue\\n        f = dict(zip(nodes, assignment))\\n        valid = True\\n        for v in nodes:\\n            if f[v] == 0:\\n                if not any(f[u] == 2 for u in G.neighbors(v)):\\n                    valid = False\\n                    break\\n        if valid:\\n            min_w = w\\n    return min_w\\n\\n# Check tight graphs\\ntight = []\\nfor n in range(2, 9):\\n    for G in nx.graph_atlas_g():\\n        if G.number_of_nodes() == n and nx.is_connected(G):\\n            rad = nx.radius(G)\\n            rdn = roman_domination_number(G)\\n            if rad + 1 > rdn:\\n                print('COUNTEREXAMPLE!', n, G.edges())\\n            elif rad + 1 == rdn:\\n                tight.append((n, rad, rdn, G.edges()))\\n\\nprint(f'Total tight graphs found: {len(tight)}')\\nfor t in tight[:10]:\\n    print(t[0], 'rad=', t[1], 'rdn=', t[2], 'edges=', list(t[3]))\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\"","RunPersistent":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Run python check for tight graphs\"","toolSummary":"\"Search tight graphs in atlas\""}}]}
